astical parts of  the story it does so in a way that feels  earned again this might just be a small  chunk of the original release but as a  standalone game Final Fantasy 7 remake  is a complete package although a great  villain lingers in the periphery of the  story cryptically alluding to something  more in clouds past and unexplained  elements are introduced in its  conclusion this doesn't diminish the  story that is told regardless of your  history with the original game Final  Fantasy 7 remake is an astounding  achievement the wait for the release was  long but in gameplay story characters  and music it delivers the weight was  worth it for first-time players it's an  opportunity to understand why Final  Fantasy 7 is held in such high regard  it's the chance to experience a  multi-faceted story that grapples with  complex subject matter be in the company  of memorable characters and be moved by  their plight for returning fans this  isn't the Final Fantasy 7 your mind  remembers it's the one your heart always  knew it to be  [Music]

